  "decision": "Cross-finger activity explains many false positives, but uniform hard-negative weighting is not the solution. Weight 2 reduces rest false-positive RMS but increases movement error and changes PCC by less than 0.001; larger weights are harmful. A future attribution model must distinguish true shared/co-movement activity from cross-finger leakage instead of treating every other-finger event as negative."
